SYNOPSIS:
        varargs void domainshout(string str, mixed domain, int regexpflag)

DESCRIPTION:
        Send a string str to all players whose environment is in the
        given domain, or if no domain is given, in the same domain as
        the outermost environment of the calling object. Messages sent
        with domainshout() won't be catched by npcs. If regexpflag is
        set and domain is of type string, domain is interpreted as
        regular expression which must match the filename of the
        players' environment.
        Note that domain can also be an array of domains in case you want
        to send a message to all players of more than one domain.

EXAMPLES:
        domainshout("Oh-oh... suddenly you hear a mighty roar.\n", "desert");
        Sends out a message to all players walking around in the desert.

        domainshout("The king is back.\n",
            "^/d/plains/myvillage/(street.*|pub|store)$", 1);
        Informs all players in certain rooms of myvillage (i.e., streets,
        the pub and the store) of the arrival of the king. Note that the
        regexp only has to match a substring of the environment unless
        you explicitely use ^ and $ as expression delimiters.

SEE ALSO:
        write(E), tell_object(E), say(E), shout(E)
